      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Conflicts between cattle and sheep interests culminated in an 1887 law favoring ranchers, while overgrazing and harsh winters like 1874‑75 depleted forage, prompting shifts toward hay production.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
